// Mastery EXERCISE 02.5 — compiles and RUNS, but misbehaves.
// `println` of a [string] array element prints the element's pointer as an
// integer, because element loads lose string-ness at the codegen level
// (unit 06 §8). Output differs run to run.
//
//   ./ionic_new examples/mastery/fail/string_array_print.ionic -o /tmp/sap && /tmp/sap

mut names = ["alice", "bob"];
println("expected: alice");
print("actual:   ");
println(names[0]);          // prints a pointer-ish integer, not "alice"

// The workaround is to copy through a plain string local first, or index an
// [int64] array (which prints correctly).
